## Visual judgement (metrics never override this)

I read both shipped PNGs with the image-read tool. The render reads as **muted olive-khaki sand with
fine pebble grain, darker cracked/scree patches and a single dry gray boulder cluster**. It visibly
satisfies R>G>B everywhere, has no green moss cast, and its dark patches are legible as relief without
black cracks. It sits in the donor desert family (L 79–114), not the bright orange reference trap.
The rock accent is a dry gray cluster, not the mossy green boulder the literal spec would have used.
Weakness: the 40×40 binary patch mask reads as rounded/blotchy camo rather than the polygonal facets
visible in donor `desert2/3` — acceptable for a single 512² piece, but a known visual gap for the
integration ticket. The compare sheet's right panel is a wooden building surface; it confirms why the
reference image must not drive palette tuning.

